-power`) | T1 gate R2 (astra) R2-06; Architect adjudication 1792960000000; refusal fixture `yang.typescript.antlr.e2e-test` pow-fractional | yang.typescript with the host-boundary seat | the follow-up that exports a host `pow` (closes PHP, Python and TS together) | P2 |\n| yang.typescript: `Number.prototype.toString(radix)` with a non-integral receiver and radix ≠ 10 (`(0.5).toString(2)`) throws a guest `TypeError` naming `G-radix-frac`; the T1 surface is Number::toString(10) plus integer radix output (T1 plan §6); fractional radix output needs V8's digit loop ported and proven host-stable | T1 gate R2 R2-07; adjudication 1792960000000; refusal fixture `e2e-test` radix-fractional | yang.typescript | the slice completing `%Number.prototype%` (T2 by §9, or a numbers follow-up) | P3 |\n| Closed (Stage 0 S3, branch yang-ts-t2b): yang.typescript ordinary functions carried no `prototype` own property; `:normal` function cells now get an eager `prototype` (writable, non-enumerable, non-configurable) with the `constructor` back-link | `object_parity_test/constructors-test` (JVM, four VMs) | yang.typescript | resolved in Stage 0 | P2 |\n| Closed (Stage 0 S3, branch yang-ts-t2b): yang.typescript every non-arrow callable was constructible; `js/is-constructor?` now reads `:kind` (`:normal`, or `:builtin` flagged `:ctor?`), so `new BigInt(1)`, `new Symbol`, `new String(x)`, arrows, methods and accessors are `TypeError` (wrapper refusal is L-T2-3) | `object_parity_test/constructors-test` | yang.typescript | resolved in Stage 0 | P3 |\n| yang.typescript: indirect eval (`(0, eval)('1')`, `globalThis.eval`) is not refused at lowering; it reaches the runtime `ReferenceError` from `js/global-get`. Direct `eval` and `new Function` refuse at lowering (T1 R2-fix) | adjudication 1792960000000 §2 R2-02 | yang.typescript | the slice that gives the global object an `eval` property, if ever; otherwise permanent | P3 |\n| Closed (Stage 0 S3, branch yang-ts-t2b): yang.typescript `%String.prototype%` had no `toString`/`valueOf`; both now answer the string | `object_parity_test/object-prototype-methods-test` | yang.typescript | resolved in Stage 0 | P3 |\n| yang.typescript: array index slots are always default data slots; `Object.defineProperty` on an index with a non-default descriptor throws `TypeError` (L-T2-1) | T2 plan R5; prelude make-array comment; `object_parity_test` descriptors | yang.typescript | the slice that gives arrays per-element descriptors, if ever | P3 |\n| yang.typescript: sparse growth beyond a gap of 2^20 holes throws `RangeError` (L-T2-2) | T2 plan R5; prelude `js/check-sparse` | yang.typescript | none scheduled | P3 |\n| yang.typescript: no wrapper objects; `new String(x)`, `new Number(x)`, `new Boolean(x)`, `Object(prim)` throw `TypeError` where Node allocates a wrapper (L-T2-3) | T2 plan R9d; corpus departures `:wrappers-*-departure` (Node `object`, pinned `TypeError`); T3 L-T3-4 inherits | yang.typescript | the slice that introduces wrapper cells, if ever | P3 |\n| yang.typescript: `Array.from` and `Object.fromEntries` accept arrays, array-likes and strings only; other iterables wait for T5 (L-T2-4) | T2 plan R10 | yang.typescript | T5 | P3 |\n| yang.typescript: `Array.prototype` methods require an array receiver; generic array-like receivers throw `TypeError` (L-T2-5) | T2 plan R10; prelude `array-definitions` | yang.typescript | none scheduled | P3 |\n| yang.typescript: `JSON.parse` ignores a reviver argument (L-T2-6) | T2 plan R11; prelude `json-definitions` | yang.typescript | a JSON follow-up or T5 | P3 |\n| yang.typescript: `%Array.prototype%` is an ordinary object, not an array exotic (L-T2-7) | T2 plan section 5; prelude `js.rt/array-proto` | yang.typescript | none scheduled | P3 |\n| yang.typescript: a function value under a computed key stays anonymous (L-T2-8) | T2 plan section 6 item 1 | yang.typescript | none scheduled | P3 |\n| yang.typescript: `console.log` of objects and arrays (the inspect subset, T2 S10) is not 