\"'ex-info (first form))\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\")\\n# namespace alias check\\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\\nPY\\nhead -48 src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"(ns yang.clojure\\n  \\\"Yang Clojure compiler - Compiles Clojure code into Yin VM Universal AST.\\n\\n  This is the Clojure-specific compiler in the Yang compiler collection.\\n  It transforms Clojure s-expressions into the Universal AST format that\\n  the Yin VM can execute. It handles:\\n  - Literals (numbers, strings, booleans, nil, collections)\\n  - Variables (symbols)\\n  - Lambda expressions (fn)\\n  - Function application (including stream operations via module system)\\n  - Conditionals (if)\\n  - Let bindings (let)\\n  - Top-level definitions via explicit yin/def store effects\\n  - Macro definitions (defmacro)\\n\\n  Macro support (docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md §10.2):\\n  - defmacro is a special form that lowers to ordinary (yin/def name (fn ...))\\n    syntax. The lambda node carries `:macro? true`, a frontend-internal fact\\n    the encoder (`yin.vm.encoder/program-batch`) turns into a declaration row;\\n    the canonical lambda row has no macro slot.\\n  - A macro call is an ordinary application. The frontend does no macro\\n    lookup: the row-native expander recognizes the call.\\n  - compile-program threads a compile-time macro-env naming the defmacros\\n    seen so far, only so the native defn lowering yields to a user defn macro.\\n\\n  Stream operations (stream/make, stream/put, stream/take, >!, <!) are compiled\\n  as regular function applications and resolved through the module system at runtime.\\n\\n  The compiler is written in .cljc format to run on both JVM and Node.js.\\\"\\n  (:refer-clojure :exclude [compile]))\\n\\n\\n;; Forward declaration for mutual recursion\\n(declare compile-form compile-lambda)\\n\\n\\n(defn literal?\\n  \\\"Check if a value is a literal (self-evaluating).\\\"\\n  [form]\\n  (or (number? form)\\n      (string? form)\\n      (true? form)\\n      (false? form)\\n      (nil? form)\\n      (keyword? form)\\n      (vector? form)\\n      (set? form)\\n      (map? form)))\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\ncollab/1793294621496-compiler-engineer-hardening2.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:23:{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_11\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"python3 - <<'PY'\\np='src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc';s=open(p).read().replace('(str/starts-with? (name (first form)) \\\\\\\".\\\\\\\")','(= \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\. (first (name (first form))))');open(p,'w').write(s)\\np='test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj';s=open(p).read()\\n# free vars context boundary only direct slot access, keep upstream pair local\\ns=s.replace(\\\\\\\"                  (= op 'quote) x\\\\\\\\n                  (and (= op 'lazy-seq)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"                  (= op 'quote) x\\n                  (and (= ns-sym 'latte_kernel.syntax) (= 'free-vars (second form))\\n                       (= x '(second def-env)))\\n                  '(second (if (map? def-env) (:definitions def-env) def-env))\\n                  (and (= op 'lazy-seq)\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\")\\ns=s.replace(\\\\\\\"    :else (kernel-rewrite ns (get top-forms [ns name]))))\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"    (and (= ns 'latte_kernel.proof)\\n         (contains? '#{elab-opaque elab-transparent install-opacity-function is-opaque?} name))\\n    (let [adapter (first (filter #(= name (second %)) context-forms))]\\n      (list* 'defn (kernel-guest-name symbol) (drop 2 adapter)))\\n    :else (kernel-rewrite ns (get top-forms [ns name]))))\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\")\\n# proof print excluded sources explicit refusal preserving graph admission rather than unresolved deps\\n# actual dispatcher opacity arms adapt updated context do\\ns=s.replace(\\\\\\\"                  (#{'fn 'fn*} op)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"                  (and (= ns-sym 'latte_kernel.proof) (= 'elab-proof-step (second form))\\n                