ierName` rejects it after a dot (corpus `:identity-object-is`, step `:G-is`, pending) | t2_packets `:identity-object-is` syntax error; T3 plan R11 | yang.typescript | T3 S0 ts-g4-2 rule (e): add `Is` to `keyword` | P2 |\\n| yang.typescript: `new X(a).m()` parses as `new (X(a).m)()` because `New singleExpression arguments` lets the operand swallow the member chain (corpus `:new-member-call`, step `:G-new`, pending) | T3 plan R11 | yang.typescript | T3 S0 ts-g4-2 rule (f): a member-expression operand for `new` | P1 |\\n| yang.php: string-offset writes (`$s[0] = 'x'`) are refused at run time with `Error \\\"string offset writes are not supported yet (yang.php known gap G-str-offset-write)\\\"`; reads are supported; row 3's single-byte writes move with this gap (`G-str-offset-write`, design 17.2 C5) | P2 plan 1.5; design 17.2 | yang.php | P9 (strings II) | P2 |\\n| yang.php: sort flags `SORT_NATURAL`, `SORT_FLAG_CASE`, `SORT_LOCALE_STRING` are refused with `Error \\\"sort flag N is not supported yet (yang.php known gap G-sort-flags)\\\"`; `SORT_REGULAR`/`NUMERIC`/`STRING` are supported (`G-sort-flags`) | P2 plan 1.9; design 17.2 | yang.php | P9 (arrays II) | P2 |\\n| yang.php: a user sort comparator that is not antisymmetric after the bool retry (for example only non-negative ints) sorts by the stable merge sort's comparison sequence, not `zend_sort`'s; the departure fixture records the walker's `[1, 2, 3]` against Zend's `[2, 1, 3]` (`G-sort-inconsistent-cmp`) | R2 adjudication R2-3; fixture `:oracle :departure`; design 17.2 | yang.php | none scheduled; reconsider if the section 14 corpus shows a real program depending on it (then P9 arrays II) | P3 |\\n| `bit-shift-right` on negative signed 64-bit integer differs on dart lane (sign extension vs arithmetic shift) | `src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:237-248`; dart lane spec §4.2 | VM core / arithmetic | post-J4 lane hardening | P2 |\\n| `BigInt` bitwise operators on JavaScript host truncate to 32-bit in specific asm.js paths | `src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:310-330` | VM core / JS host | post-J4 lane hardening | P3 |\\n| Mixed lock families: a Node session holding a store directory via its `lock.<pid>.<nonce>` claim file and an OS-lock host (jolt — from J4b — JVM, Dart) holding via fcntl are invisible to each other; simultaneous use of one store directory across the two families can double-own and corrupt. Sequential reopen is unaffected and tested. Pre-existing between JVM and Node; jolt inherits it, does not create it. JVM/Dart/jolt mutual exclusion via fcntl IS enforced and gated. | J4 design §3 cross-host limit; fable J4 review F5; owner ruling 2026-10-25 \\\"document it\\\" (option a of the three-way: record, best-effort refusal, or common-lock design) | jolt lane (J4b) | documented limitation — the ledger row is the fix. A future common-lock design (option c) would supersede; the best-effort Node-claim refusal (option b) remains available as an enhancement if the accident ever occurs in practice. J4b's acceptance must not claim universal cross-runtime exclusion | P2 |\\n| Closed (J4b): `dao.space.store.fs` on jolt — the directory lock (`FileChannel.tryLock` failed: journals answered `:locked`), `StandardCharsets/UTF_8` decoding, and the dangling-symlink refusal of `read-bounded` (fs_test.cljc:98) did not work, so `dao.space.store.fs-test` was excluded from the jolt lane (this row restates the J4 row the 4d6fd818 merge dropped) | J4 design §2-§5; commissioning collab/1792948716498; J4b collab/1792948716498-engineer-j4b-directory-locks.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md | jolt lane (J4b) | closed: `:jolt` arms over `dao.posix.file` / native/jolt-file layout 2: whole-file `fcntl(F_SETLK)` write lock, close-on-exec, released by its one close, `held` unchanged in fs.cljc; realpath; HEAD temp O_EXCL 0666 & ~umask → write-all → fsync → checked close → before-rename → rename → directory open+fsync+close (`directory-sync-supported?` true, a sync error fails the replacement); bounded reads classify + O_NONBLOCK + fstat recheck; strict UTF-8 via `text.jolt`. `bb probe:jolt-file` gates 1-6 (jolt↔jolt, jolt↔JVM both ways, jolt↔Dart both ways, SIGKILL recovery, O_CLOEXEC in an exec'd child, HEAD cut matrix with injected directory-sync failure, bounded reads) and the hygiene re-run; `dao.space.store.fs-test` rejoined `test:jolt-core`. JVM/Dart/jolt mutual exclusion via fcntl IS enforced and gated; the mixed Node/OS-lock row above stands | closed |\\n| yang.php: a by-reference variadic parameter (`function f(&...$xs)`) is refused at lowering as `:variadic-reference` (C24, `G-variadic-by-ref`); by-value variadics, named extras and spread are supported | P3 plan section 5; Stage 0 gate (collab/1793020431000) D1; `e2e-test/refusals-are-named-test` | yang.php | P9 | P2 |\\n| yang.php: a spread with string keys (`f(...['a' => 1])`) is refused at run time with `Error \\\"spread with string keys is not supported yet (yang.php known gap G-spread-string-keys)\\\"` (C25); PHP binds the keys as named arguments, so row 65 is not claimed at program level; fixture `:call-spread-string-key-gap` (oracle-only, pending the next shiva pass) | Stage 0 gate D2; `e2e-test/gate-fix-programs-test` | yang.php | P4 (row 65 lands with `pcall-arg-named`) | P2 |\\n| yang.php: by-reference `foreach` keeps an ordinal and re-reads the location each iteration (C26, `G-foreach-iterator-registry`); the same-table clause of rows 25 and 26 is implemented, the copy-hit and unrelated clauses of row 25, the rebuild clause of row 26 and rows 54, 60 and 61 are not (`sort($a)` or `$a = [..]` inside the loop differ from PHP); `fe-next` is a linear scan per iteration; fixtures `:foreach-ref-sort-inside-loop` and `:foreach-ref-array-reassigned-in-loop` (oracle-only, pending) | Stage 0 gate D3; design 17.2 C26 | yang.php | P3-c (iterator registry, the P3 plan's S7.2 and S7.3), before P4-b lands row 29 | P2 |\\n| yang.php: the vendored `PhpParser.g4` reads `fn($x)` as a call to a function named `fn` and `[fn($x) => ...]` as a