| P3-c (iterator registry, the P3 plan's S7.2 and S7.3), before P4-b lands row 29 | P2 |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:115:| yang.php: the vendored `PhpParser.g4` reads `fn($x)` as a call to a function named `fn` and `[fn($x) => ...]` as a key/value pair, and has no `foreach (... as $k => [$x, $y])`; the held fixtures `:call-dynamic-dim` and `:foreach-key-and-destructure` keep their recorded oracle values and flip on with a grammar patch (C27, `G-grammar-fn-item`) | Stage 0 gate D4; vendored grammar byte-identical to upstream `85e2dd17` | yang.php | a grammar-patch slice through the manifest `:patches` mechanism, regenerated on every target, before or inside P4 S0 | P2 |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:116:| yang.php: member calls go through one `php/method-call` seam (`getMessage`, `getCode`, `getPrevious` on Throwable; `bindTo`, `__invoke` on Closure); `bindTo` shares statics with the source closure (PHP copies them); `new` and classes are refused; the call protocol validates a named argument's name at entry, so in `f(1, z: 2, w: side())` `side()` runs where PHP stops at `z` (C28, `G-method-seam`); fixture `:call-unknown-named-later-arg-runs` (oracle-only, pending) | Stage 0 gate D5 and section 3; `e2e-test/gate-fix-programs-test` | yang.php | P4 S2 (class model) and P4 S4 (`pcall-begin/arg/enter` with `new`) | P2 |\\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:117:| yang.php: `var_dump` of a self-referencing array prints `*RECURSION*` at the re-entry (a visited path of instance-array cell ids) and `==`, `===` on cyclic arrays raise `Error \\\"Nesting level too deep - recursive dependency?\\\"` after a depth of 100 (C29, `G-recursion-guard`); the exact PHP texts are recorded by the fixtures `:ref-cycle-var-dump` and `:ref-cycle-compare` (pending the next shiva pass); `print_r`, `json_encode`, `var_export`, `serialize` are unsupported builtins | Stage 0 gate D7, adjudication X2; `prelude-test/gate-cycle-guard-test` | yang.php | the P4-seam oracle run pins the texts | P2 |\\ndocs/agents/kn