\\"completed\\\"}}\\ncollab/1793294621496-compiler-engineer-hardening2.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:182:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_95\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"tail -8 /tmp/h2-oracle-final.log; cat > test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md <<'MD'\\\\n# Slice 9 kernel differential gate — BLOCKED\\\\n\\\\nHardening program 2 implementation round, based on \\\\\\\"'`7dc18478`. This is an\\\\nimplementation evidence report, not the final verification slice or a\\\\nconformance certificate. The close-out assertion remains red.\\\\n\\\\nThe baseline had 54 fixtures: **4 passing, 2 mismatches, 48 blocked**. The same\\\\n54 fixtures now have **50 passing, 2 mismatches, 2 blocked**. Three additional\\\\nfixtures exercise explicit fresh-supply rebuilding and the real proof dispatcher'\\\\\\\"'s\\\\nopacity transitions and refusal. The complete current result is **53 passing,\\\\n2 mismatches, 2 blocked, 57 attempted, 0 skipped**.\\\\n\\\\nEvery fixture has independent A, B, C-walker and C-semantic records in\\\\n[\\\\\\\"'`slice9_evidence.edn`](slice9_evidence.edn). Each passing row additionally\\\\nrecords explicit A/B, A/C-walker, A/C-semantic and C/C agreement flags. No host\\\\nparser, normalizer, type checker, proof dispatcher or extension callback replaces\\\\nguest execution. The assume/have/discharge proof passes within the unchanged\\\\n1,000,000-instruction limit on both C lanes.\\\\n\\\\n## Admission denominator\\\\n\\\\nThe regenerated manifest contains 155 bindings: **146 admitted, 9 excluded**.\\\\nIts 147 functions have 175 candidate function/arity entries: **165 admitted,\\\\n10 excluded**. Exclusions name clock access, host pprint/output capture, and\\\\nfunctions that directly use those diagnostics. Their guest entry points raise\\\\nan explicit nonportable-binding refusal if reached; excluding a diagnostic\\\\nbinding does not exclude the proof dispatcher that contains a diagnostic arm.\\\\n\\\\nThe proven direct A/B/C execution count is **22/165 admitted arities**. The\\\\nremaining **143** admitted entries are individually listed under\\\\n`:coverage :unexercised`. Transitive execution coverage remains **unproven**;\\\\nsource dependency membership never substitutes for execution. Fixture success\\\\ndoes not narrow the admission denominator. These obligations independently keep\\\\nthe final gate open.\\\\n\\\\nRegenerate admission decisions and the existing derived throw/case tables with:\\\\n\\\\n```sh\\\\nclj -X:test:dev latte-oracle-tables/-main\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Closed dependencies and explicit conventions\\\\n\\\\n- Guest implementations admit `butlast`, `last`, bare `nth`, `string?`, `update`,\\\\n  and callable collections; the compiler lowers `->` through ordinary control\\\\n  forms. Callable collections use the guest library, with ordinary closures\\\\n  taking the direct callable path.\\\\n- `kind/var?` explicitly admits the JVM Clojure Var predicate. Namespace lookup\\\\n  still requires a separately installed host capability.\\\\n- Metadata attachment uses a declared pure **`kind/with-meta` seam**. This is a\\\\n  departure from the requested guest-only implementation: metadata is carried\\\\n  on existing host symbols/collections, and the current `data` module exposes\\\\n  no operation that can attach it. Introducing a second tagged representation\\\\n  would change symbol identity and every collection boundary. No Yin source or\\\\n  ABI was changed; domain metadata is checked by the existing shape comparison.\\\\n- Fresh allocation consumes immutable `{:counter N}` data and returns\\\\n  `[symbol next-supply]`, constructing `G__<prefix><N>`. The original A call\\\\n  `(let [a (gensym \\\\\\\"fresh\\\\\\\") b (gensym \\\\\\\"fresh\\\\\\\")] (= a b))` returns false.\\\\n  B/C thread the supply explicitly through the corresponding two allocations,\\\\n  also returning false. Prefix-only ambient allocation is refused; no hidden\\\\n  mutable counter is installed. Numeric deterministic constructors remain\\\\n  compatible with slice 8. `rebuild-type` returns `[original-result next-context]`,\\\\n  and its proof caller binds that next context explicitly.\\\\n- The free-vars argument boundary extracts the original global/local definition\\\\n  pair from `:definitions` before entering the upstream body. Its original\\\\n  `(second def-env)` access is preserved; local capture now returns `#{x}` on A,\\\\n  B and both C lanes.\\\\n- The actual `typing/unfold-implicit` source runs through portable `try/catch`.\\\\n  Throws retain early-return outcomes; exception bindings carry error data;\\\\n  `.getMessage`, `ex-message`, and `ex-data` access that data. Both the typed and\\\\n  throwing guest extension fixtures pass. Unsupported host accessors such as\\\\n  `.getStackTrace` are refused at compile time and recorded in the evidence.\\\\n- The former opacity atom names the explicit `:opacity-policy` context field.\\\\n  Installation returns an updated context. The real upstream proof dispatcher\\\\n  threads that context through opaque/transparent arms; the two added opacity\\\\n  fixtures pass without substituting slice 8'\\\\\\\"'s restricted dispatcher.\\\\n\\\\nObserver exceptions can attach an entire host VM session. Evidence records\\\\nwhether that diagnostic snapshot was attached and retains its exception data\\\\nand causes, without recursively expanding the VM's duplicated closure\\\\n environments. It does not remove domain error payloads.\\\\n\\\\n## Remaining mismatches with minimal repros\\\\n\\\\nBoth mismatches arise from upstream placing the **host \\\\\\\"'`clojure.core/meta`\\\\nfunction itself** in after-qed error data. A and B retain that nonportable host\\\\nvalue; C carries its guest closure. This difference is not accepted or erased.\\\\n\\\\n```clojure\\\\n;; :elab-after-qed\\\\n(latte-kernel.proof/elab-proof env []\\\\n  '\\\\\\\"'[[:qed (lambda [A :type] (lambda [x A] x)) {}]\\\\n    [:qed missing {}]])\\\\n\\\\n;; :check-after-qed\\\\n(latte-kernel.proof/check-proof env [] 'late '✳\\\\n  '[[:qed (lambda [A :type] (lambda [x A] x)) {}]\\\\n    [:qed missing {}]])\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```\\\\n\\\\nThe two remaining blockers are upstream failures, not accepted negative results:\\\\n\\\\n```clojure\\\\n;; :typing-ascription — pinned upstream declares type-of-ascribe but never\\\\n;; defines it. A raises an unbound-function error; B/C refuse that exact branch.\\\\n(latte-kernel.typing/type-of-term env '\\\\\\\"'[[A ✳] [x A]]\\\\n  '(:latte-kernel.syntax/ascribe x A))\\\\n\\\\n;; :compile-malformed — A and B raise native scalar-sequence exceptions.\\\\n;; C returns a portable sequence refusal, which is not counted as agreement.\\\\n(latte-kernel.proof/compile-proof '[42])\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```\\\\n\\\\n## Verification\\\\n\\\\nThe required compiler, macro, stream-eval and store-write-audit regression suites\\\\npass: **122 tests, 1,337 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\\\\n\\\\n```sh\\\\nclj -M:test -n yang.clojure-test -n yin.vm.macro-test '\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  -n yang.clojure.stream-eval-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test\\\\nclj -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```\\\\n\\\\nThe oracle suite retains exactly the expected close-out gate failure; the other\\\\noracle tests pass. The manifest schema and gate assertions check dispositions,\\\\nthe admitted/excluded partition, unique fixture execution, negative outcomes,\\\\nand agreement records. Clj-kondo reports **0 errors, 2 inherited warnings, no new\\\\nwarnings**. Cljstyle and `git diff --check` pass.\\\\n\\\\nThe stream suite'\\\\\\\"'s generated-parser prerequisites were rebuilt locally from\\\\ncopied immutable cached inputs, with the repository generator checking all\\\\npinned input and generated-source digests. No other checkout's mutable build\\\\noutputs are shared. The acceptance above executes both C evaluators on the JVM;\\\\nit does not claim a new Node or Dart host verification run.\\\\n\\\\nThe pinned upstream revision is \\\\\\\"'`86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279`.\\\\nThe evidence records the base compiler/VM revision, exact compiler source SHA-256,\\\\nhost versions, context/assembly adaptation version 2, unchanged instruction\\\\nbudget, admission inventory, and dependency graph. Normal tests do not rewrite\\\\nchecked-in evidence; explicit refresh uses\\\\n`yang.latte-oracle-test/write-kernel-gate-evidence!`.\\\\nMD\\\\npython3 - <<'\\\\\\\"'PY'\\\\np='test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md';s=open(p).read().replace('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n environments.', '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nenvironments.');open(p,'w').write(s)\\\\nPY\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\ncollab/1793294621496-compiler-engineer-hardening2.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:183:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_95\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"tail -8 /tmp/h2-oracle-final.log; cat > test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md <<'MD'\\\\n# Slice 9 kernel differential gate — BLOCKED\\\\n\\\\nHardening program 2 implementation round, based on \\\\\\\"'`7dc18478`. This is an\\\\nimplementation evidence report, not the final verification slice or a\\\\nconformance certificate. The close-out assertion remains red.\\\\n\\\\nThe baseline had 54 fixtures: **4 passing, 2 mismatches, 48 blocked**. The same\\\\n54 fixtures now have **50 passing, 2 mismatches, 2 blocked**. Three additional\\\\nfixtures exercise explicit fresh-supply rebuilding and the real proof dispatcher'\\\\\\\"'s\\\\nopacity transitions and refusal. The complete current result is **53 passing,\\\\n2 mismatches, 2 blocked, 57 attempted, 0 skipped**.\\\\n\\\\nEvery fixture has independent A, B, C-walker and C-semantic records in\\\\n[\\\\\\\"'`slice9_evidence.edn`](slice9_evidence.edn). Each passing row additionally\\\\nrecords explicit A/B, A/C-walker, A/C-semantic and C/C agreement flags. No host\\\\nparser, normalizer, type checker, proof dispatcher or extension callback replaces\\\\nguest execution. The assume/have/discharge proof passes within the unchanged\\\\n1,000,000-instruction limit on both C lanes.\\\\n\\\\n## Admission denominator\\\\n\\\\nThe regenerated manifest contains 155 bindings: **146 admitted, 9 excluded**.\\\\nIts 147 functions have 175 candidate function/arity entries: **165 admitted,\\\\n10 excluded**. Exclusions name clock access, host pprint/output capture, and\\\\nfunctions that directly use those diagnostics. Their guest entry points raise\\\\nan explicit nonportable-binding refusal if reached; excluding a diagnostic\\\\nbinding does not exclude the proof dispatcher that contains a diagnostic arm.\\\\n\\\\nThe proven direct A/B/C execution count is **22/165 admitted arities**. The\\\\nremaining **143** admitted entries are individually listed under\\\\n`:coverage :unexercised`. Transitive execution coverage remains **unproven**;\\\\nsource dependency membership never substitutes for execution. Fixture success\\\\ndoes not narrow the admission denominator. These obligations independently keep\\\\nthe final gate open.\\\\n\\\\nRegenerate admission decisions and the existing derived throw/case tables with:\\\\n\\\\n```sh\\\\nclj -X:test:dev latte-oracle-tables/-main\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n## Closed dependencies and explicit conventions\\\\n\\\\n- Guest implementations admit `butlast`, `last`, bare `nth`, `string?`, `update`,\\\\n  and callable collections; the compiler lowers `->` through ordinary control\\\\n  forms. Callable collections use the guest library, with ordinary closures\\\\n  taking the direct callable path.\\\\n- `kind/var?` explicitly admits the JVM Clojure Var predicate. Namespace lookup\\\\n  still requires a separately installed host capability.\\\\n- Metadata attachment uses a declared pure **`kind/with-meta` seam**. This is a\\\\n  departure from the requested guest-only implementation: metadata is carried\\\\n  on existing host symbols/collections, and the current `data` module exposes\\\\n  no operation that can attach it. Introducing a second tagged representation\\\\n  would change symbol identity and every collection boundary. No Yin source or\\\\n  ABI was changed; domain metadata is checked by the existing shape comparison.\\\\n- Fresh allocation consumes immutable `{:counter N}` data and returns\\\\n  `[symbol next-supply]`, constructing `G__<prefix><N>`. The original A call\\\\n  `(let [a (gensym \\\\\\\"fresh\\\\\\\") b (gensym \\\\\\\"fresh\\\\\\\")] (= a b))` returns false.\\\\n  B/C thread the supply explicitly through the corresponding two allocations,\\\\n  also returning false. Prefix-only ambient allocation is refused; no hidden\\\\n  mutable counter is installed. Numeric deterministic constructors remain\\\\n  compatible with slice 8. `rebuild-type` returns `[original-result next-context]`,\\\\n  and its proof caller binds that next context explicitly.\\\\n- The free-vars argument boundary extracts the original global/local definition\\\\n  pair from `:definitions` before entering the upstream body. Its original\\\\n  `(second def-env)` access is preserved; local capture now returns `#{x}` on A,\\\\n  B and both C lanes.\\\\n- The actual `typing/unfold-implicit` source runs through portable `try/catch`.\\\\n  Throws retain early-return outcomes; exception bindings carry error data;\\\\n  `.getMessage`, `ex-message`, and `ex-data` access that data. Both the typed and\\\\n  throwing guest extension fixtures pass. Unsupported host accessors such as\\\\n  `.getStackTrace` are refused at compile time and recorded in the evidence.\\\\n- The former opacity atom names the explicit `:opacity-policy` context field.\\\\n  Installation returns an updated context. The real upstream proof dispatcher\\\\n  threads that context through opaque/transparent arms; the two added opacity\\\\n  fixtures pass without substituting slice 8'\\\\\\\"'s restricted dispatcher.\\\\n\\\\nObserver exceptions can attach an entire host VM session. Evidence records\\\\nwhether that diagnostic snapshot was attached and retains its exception data\\\\nand causes, without recursively expanding the VM's duplicated closure\\\\n environments. It does not remove domain error payloads.\\\\n\\\\n## Remaining mismatches with minimal repros\\\\n\\\\nBoth mismatches arise from upstream placing the **host \\\\\\\"'`clojure.core/meta`\\\\nfunction itself** in after-qed error data. A and B retain that nonportable host\\\\nvalue; C carries its guest closure. This difference is not accepted or erased.\\\\n\\\\n```clojure\\\\n;; :elab-after-qed\\\\n(latte-kernel.proof/elab-proof env []\\\\n  '\\\\\\\"'[[:qed (lambda [A :type] (lambda [x A] x)) {}]\\\\n    [:qed missing {}]])\\\\n\\\\n;; :check-after-qed\\\\n(latte-kernel.proof/check-proof env [] 'late '✳\\\\n  '[[:qed (lambda [A :type] (lambda [x A] x)) {}]\\\\n    [:qed missing {}]])\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```\\\\n\\\\nThe two remaining blockers are upstream failures, not accepted negative results:\\\\n\\\\n```clojure\\\\n;; :typing-ascription — pinned upstream declares type-of-ascribe but never\\\\n;; defines it. A raises an unbound-function error; B/C refuse that exact branch.\\\\n(latte-kernel.typing/type-of-term env '\\\\\\\"'[[A ✳] [x A]]\\\\n  '(:latte-kernel.syntax/ascribe x A))\\\\n\\\\n;; :compile-malformed — A and B raise native scalar-sequence exceptions.\\\\n;; C returns a portable sequence refusal, which is not counted as agreement.\\\\n(latte-kernel.proof/compile-proof '[42])\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```\\\\n\\\\n## Verification\\\\n\\\\nThe required compiler, macro, stream-eval and store-write-audit regression suites\\\\npass: **122 tests, 1,337 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\\\\n\\\\n```sh\\\\nclj -M:test -n yang.clojure-test -n yin.vm.macro-test '\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n  -n yang.clojure.stream-eval-test -n yin.vm.store-write-audit-test\\\\nclj -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test\\\\n\\\\\\\"'```\\\\n\\\\nThe oracle suite retains exactly the expected close-out gate failure; the other\\\\noracle tests pass. The manifest schema and gate assertions check dispositions,\\\\nthe admitted/excluded partition, unique fixture execution, negative outcomes,\\\\nand agreement records. Clj-kondo reports **0 errors, 2 inherited warnings, no new\\\\nwarnings**. Cljstyle and `git diff --check` pass.\\\\n\\\\nThe stream suite'\\\\\\\"'s generated-parser prerequisites were rebuilt locally from\\\\ncopied immutable cached inputs, with the repository generator checking all\\\\npinned input and generated-source digests. No other checkout's mutable build\\\\noutputs are shared. The acceptance above executes both C evaluators on the JVM;\\\\nit does not claim a new Node or Dart host verification run.\\\\n\\\\nThe pinned upstream revision is \\\\\\\"'`86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279`.\\\\nThe evidence records the base compiler/VM revision, exact compiler source SHA-256,\\\\nhost versions, context/assembly adaptation version 2, unchanged instruction\\\\nbudget, admission inventory, and dependency graph. Normal tests do not rewrite\\\\nchecked-in evidence; explicit refresh uses\\\\n`yang.latte-oracle-test/write-kernel-gate-evidence!`.\\\\nMD\\\\npython3 - <<'\\\\\\\"'PY'\\\\np='test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_gate.md';s=open(p).read().replace('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n environments.', '\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\nenvironments.');open(p,'w').write(s)\\\\nPY\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"Kernel gate remains blocked: {:pass 53, :blocked 2, :mismatch 2}; admitted/candidate but unexercised function/arities=143. See slice9_evidence.edn; blocked fixtures are not accepted negatives.\\\\nexpected: (= :pass (:gate-status evidence))\\\\n  actual: (not (= :pass :blocked))\\\\nORACLE latte-kernel.defenv/mkenv A= [[] {}] C= {:status :ok, :value [[] {}]}\\\\nORACLE latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? A= true C= {:status :ok, :value true}\\\\n\\\\nRan 23 tests containing 997 assertions.\\\\n1 failures, 0 errors.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ncollab/1793294621496-compiler-engineer-hardening2.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:209:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.started\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_109\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"cat > /tmp/h2-commit-message.txt <<'TXT'\\\\nfix(yang.clojure): close kernel hardening dependency blockers\\\\n\\\\nRecord manifest admission dispositions and admit missing guest operations.\\\\nLower portable try/catch and thread fresh-name and opacity contexts explicitly.\\\\n\\\\nRaise fixture agreement from 4/54 to 53/57 while retaining the blocked gate,\\\\ntwo named mismatches, two upstream failures and unproven arity coverage.\\\\nDocument the explicit-supply and metadata representation seams.\\\\n\\\\nValidation: 145 tests, 2335 assertions, zero errors and only the expected\\\\nclose-out gate failure. Regression suites pass; kondo has zero errors and\\\\nno new warnings.\\\\nTXT\\\\n git diff --cached --check\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":null,\\\"status\\\":\\\"in_progress\\\"}}\\ncollab/1793294621496-compiler-engineer-hardening2.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:210:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_109\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"cat > /tmp/h2-commit-message.txt <<'TXT'\\\\nfix(yang.clojure): close kernel hardening dependency blockers\\\\n\\\\nRecord manifest admission dispositions and admit missing guest operations.\\\\nLower portable try/catch and thread fresh-name and opacity contexts explicitly.\\\\n\\\\nRaise fixture agreement from 4/54 to 53/57 while retaining the blocked gate,\\\\ntwo named mismatches, two upstream failures and unproven arity coverage.\\\\nDocument the explicit-supply and metadata representation seams.\\\\n\\\\nValidation: 145 tests, 2335 assertions, zero errors and only the expected\\\\nclose-out gate failure. Regression suites pass; kondo has zero errors and\\\\nno new warnings.\\\\nTXT\\\\n git diff --cached --check\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.stdout.log:7:**Verdict: the round's claims are substantiated.** The 4→50 pass improvement on the unchanged 54-fixture baseline is produced by real guest machinery, not loosened fixtures; the admission inventory is sound and conservatively defaults new bindings to admitted; the 143 unexercised arities are honest accounting that independently keeps the gate open. Four P3 findings below; no P0–P2. The requested judgment on the kind/`var?` + `with-meta` departure: **justified, with two carried obligations**.\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.stdout.log:11:**P3 | src/dev/latte_oracle_manifest.clj:50-57** | The stale manifest generator still rewrites `test/yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn` in the old schema (no `:disposition`/`:admission-reason`), while `latte-oracle-tables/-main` (src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj:48-51) is now the writer of record. Running the old tool per its own docstring (`clj -M -m latte-oracle-manifest`) wipes the admission inventory from the working tree; the schema assertion in `test-oracle-classification` (test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:281-283) then fails loudly, but the checked-in inventory is lost and the old header comment is now false. | Fix: delete `latte-oracle-manifest` or reduce it to a delegation to `latte-oracle-tables`, and update its docstring.\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.stdout.log:13:**P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:895-919** | The portable `try` lowerer's catch arm fires on *any* `[error-tag v]`: it binds `(data/nth outcome 1)` (line ~912) without discriminating the thrown value. A thrown non-ex-info value (e.g. `(throw \\\"boom\\\")` inside `(try … (catch Exception e …))`) is caught by the guest but propagates in Clojure (a thrown String is not an Exception). The catch-class guard (lines 903-905) constrains only the *syntax* of the clause, not the runtime class of the thrown value. Unexercised: all kernel sources throw ex-info only, and `test-portable-try-outcomes` (test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2024) tests ex-info throws exclusively. | Fix: either record the limitation in the library notes next to the other \\\"known compromises\\\" (clojure.cljc:1908-1916), or discriminate at runtime (catch only values carrying `:yin.k/message`, re-propagating others).\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.stdout.log:15:**P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1163-1166** | Callable collections route through `invoke-value` only when the operator is a **local** or a **non-symbol** (`(or (contains? (locals env) operator) (not (symbol? operator)))`). A top-level defined collection — `(def v [1 2]) (v 0)` — compiles to a plain `:application` and errors at runtime instead of indexing, diverging from Clojure. Untested boundary of the \\\"callable collections\\\" admission (test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2049 uses only `let`-bound collections). | Fix: record as a known boundary in the library notes, or extend the route to operators in `::defined`.\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.stdout.log:17:**P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1918-1926** | `kind-arities` publishes `'var? [1]` unconditionally (line 1926) while `kind-module` provides `var?` only under `#?(:clj … :default {})` (line 1920) — on a Node/Dart host the arity profile would admit a binding the module cannot supply. Relatedly, metadata attached via the new `kind/with-meta` seam has no stated serialization-survival guarantee: no fixture round-trips a meta'd value through the store/encoder, so `meta` after restoration is unspecified. | Fix: gate the published arity with the same reader conditional (or register the capability per-host at harness setup), and add a note/obligation that host metadata is not a serialized ABI field.\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.stdout.log:37:7. **143 unexercised arities.** Honest: `direct` counts only `:pass` rows' original calls (latte_oracle_test.clj:1746-1752); the denominator is the disposition inventory independent of fixture success; 165 − 22 = 143, each listed under `:coverage :unexercised`; the admitted+excluded partition of the 175 candidates is asserted (line 1831-1833). The only denominator shrinkage vs baseline is the 10 excluded arities — the disclosed admission change itself. The close-out test deliberately asserts `:pass` against a `:blocked` reality, keeping the suite red until the gate truly closes.\\ncollab/1793294621496-compiler-engineer-hardening2.prompt.md:15:- test/yang/latte_oracle/ (manifest admission dispositions + fixture additions)\\ncollab/1793294621496-compiler-engineer-hardening2.prompt.md:23:1. MANIFEST ADMISSION DISPOSITIONS: the manifest (test/yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn) records no admitted/excluded dispositions (the gate recorded :not-recorded-in-inherited-manifest). Extend the manifest schema and src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj so every binding carries :disposition :admitted | :excluded + :admission-reason, regenerate the table, and make the gate's coverage denominator read it. Admitted = reachable through the guest library + data module + admitted host seams (kind/*); excluded = genuinely nonportable (nano-time, pprint, host interop) with reasons. The gate-report format gains an honest admitted-vs-excluded denominator.\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.prompt.md:17:dispositions (schema + regeneration + denominator), stdlib admissions (butlast/last/nth/\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.prompt.md:30:(.getMessage/ex-data paths); the meta-host-value mismatch disposition (upstream deviation\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.prompt.md:38:Report findings as: P0-P3 | file:line | evidence | fix. State \\\"No actionable findings\\\"\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.findings.md:6:**Verdict: the round's claims are substantiated.** The 4→50 pass improvement on the unchanged 54-fixture baseline is produced by real guest machinery, not loosened fixtures; the admission inventory is sound and conservatively defaults new bindings to admitted; the 143 unexercised arities are honest accounting that independently keeps the gate open. Four P3 findings below; no P0–P2. The requested judgment on the kind/`var?` + `with-meta` departure: **justified, with two carried obligations**.\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.findings.md:10:**P3 | src/dev/latte_oracle_manifest.clj:50-57** | The stale manifest generator still rewrites `test/yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn` in the old schema (no `:disposition`/`:admission-reason`), while `latte-oracle-tables/-main` (src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj:48-51) is now the writer of record. Running the old tool per its own docstring (`clj -M -m latte-oracle-manifest`) wipes the admission inventory from the working tree; the schema assertion in `test-oracle-classification` (test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:281-283) then fails loudly, but the checked-in inventory is lost and the old header comment is now false. | Fix: delete `latte-oracle-manifest` or reduce it to a delegation to `latte-oracle-tables`, and update its docstring.\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.findings.md:12:**P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:895-919** | The portable `try` lowerer's catch arm fires on *any* `[error-tag v]`: it binds `(data/nth outcome 1)` (line ~912) without discriminating the thrown value. A thrown non-ex-info value (e.g. `(throw \\\"boom\\\")` inside `(try … (catch Exception e …))`) is caught by the guest but propagates in Clojure (a thrown String is not an Exception). The catch-class guard (lines 903-905) constrains only the *syntax* of the clause, not the runtime class of the thrown value. Unexercised: all kernel sources throw ex-info only, and `test-portable-try-outcomes` (test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2024) tests ex-info throws exclusively. | Fix: either record the limitation in the library notes next to the other \\\"known compromises\\\" (clojure.cljc:1908-1916), or discriminate at runtime (catch only values carrying `:yin.k/message`, re-propagating others).\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.findings.md:14:**P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1163-1166** | Callable collections route through `invoke-value` only when the operator is a **local** or a **non-symbol** (`(or (contains? (locals env) operator) (not (symbol? operator)))`). A top-level defined collection — `(def v [1 2]) (v 0)` — compiles to a plain `:application` and errors at runtime instead of indexing, diverging from Clojure. Untested boundary of the \\\"callable collections\\\" admission (test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2049 uses only `let`-bound collections). | Fix: record as a known boundary in the library notes, or extend the route to operators in `::defined`.\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.findings.md:16:**P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1918-1926** | `kind-arities` publishes `'var? [1]` unconditionally (line 1926) while `kind-module` provides `var?` only under `#?(:clj … :default {})` (line 1920) — on a Node/Dart host the arity profile would admit a binding the module cannot supply. Relatedly, metadata attached via the new `kind/with-meta` seam has no stated serialization-survival guarantee: no fixture round-trips a meta'd value through the store/encoder, so `meta` after restoration is unspecified. | Fix: gate the published arity with the same reader conditional (or register the capability per-host at harness setup), and add a note/obligation that host metadata is not a serialized ABI field.\\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.findings.md:36:7. **143 unexercised arities.** Honest: `direct` counts only `:pass` rows' original calls (latte_oracle_test.clj:1746-1752); the denominator is the disposition inventory independent of fixture success; 165 − 22 = 143, each listed under `:coverage :unexercised`; the admitted+excluded partition of the 175 candidates is asserted (line 1831-1833). The only denominator shrinkage vs baseline is the 10 excluded arities — the disclosed admission change itself. The close-out test deliberately asserts `:pass` against a `:blocked` reality, keeping the suite red until the gate truly closes.\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' -g '*format.md' -g '*hardening*' -g '*architect*' && rg -n 'rebuild-type|elab-have|elab-declare|def-env\\\\\\\\x27|fresh' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg --files -g 'AGENTS.md' -g '*format.md' -g '*hardening*' -g '*architect*' && rg -n 'rebuild-type|elab-have|elab-declare|def-env\\\\\\\\x27|fresh' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"AGENTS.md\\npublic/chp/blog/yin-vm-daospace-architecture.blog\\npublic/chp/blog/architecture.blog\\npublic/chp/blog/php-security-by-architecture.blog\\npublic/chp/blog/stream-vs-interface-architecture.blog\\norchestrator-logs/1793187400000-glm-yang-clojure-hardening.md\\norchestrator-logs/1793192500000-glm-resume-yang-clojure-hardening.md\\norchestrator-logs/1793188658-yang-clojure-hardening-claude.md\\narchive/yin-ucf/1789932043826-architect-debruijn-d0d1-signoff.prompt.md\\narchive/yin-ucf/1789391552000-architect-ucf-revision-r3.glm-5-3.stdout.log\\narchive/yin-ucf/1791500000000-architect-ucf-transport-tuples-review-r4.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md\\narchive/yin-ucf/1789717046000-architect-review-u16.prompt.md\\narchive/yin-ucf/1791500000000-architect-ucf-transport-tuples-review-r4.prompt.md\\narchive/yin-ucf/1791275000000-architect-d10