{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'DENIED|def-env.|closing|disposition|P2' collab/*prompt.md collab/*findings.md\"","aggregated_output":"collab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.findings.md:6:**Verdict: the round's claims are substantiated.** The 4→50 pass improvement on the unchanged 54-fixture baseline is produced by real guest machinery, not loosened fixtures; the admission inventory is sound and conservatively defaults new bindings to admitted; the 143 unexercised arities are honest accounting that independently keeps the gate open. Four P3 findings below; no P0–P2. The requested judgment on the kind/`var?` + `with-meta` departure: **justified, with two carried obligations**.\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.findings.md:10:**P3 | src/dev/latte_oracle_manifest.clj:50-57** | The stale manifest generator still rewrites `test/yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn` in the old schema (no `:disposition`/`:admission-reason`), while `latte-oracle-tables/-main` (src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj:48-51) is now the writer of record. Running the old tool per its own docstring (`clj -M -m latte-oracle-manifest`) wipes the admission inventory from the working tree; the schema assertion in `test-oracle-classification` (test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:281-283) then fails loudly, but the checked-in inventory is lost and the old header comment is now false. | Fix: delete `latte-oracle-manifest` or reduce it to a delegation to `latte-oracle-tables`, and update its docstring.\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.findings.md:33:4. **free-vars restoration.** The upstream body is verbatim (its `(second def-env)` preserved; upstream syntax.cljc:204-228); the only addition is an argument-boundary `let` unwrapping a context map to its `:definitions` pair (latte_oracle_test.clj:1422-1429), accepting both shapes.\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.glm-5.3.findings.md:36:7. **143 unexercised arities.** Honest: `direct` counts only `:pass` rows' original calls (latte_oracle_test.clj:1746-1752); the denominator is the disposition inventory independent of fixture success; 165 − 22 = 143, each listed under `:coverage :unexercised`; the admitted+excluded partition of the 175 candidates is asserted (line 1831-1833). The only denominator shrinkage vs baseline is the 10 excluded arities — the disclosed admission change itself. The close-out test deliberately asserts `:pass` against a `:blocked` reality, keeping the suite red until the gate truly closes.\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.prompt.md:13:round 1, closing the slice-9 gate's blockers. Read the gate report\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.prompt.md:17:dispositions (schema + regeneration + denominator), stdlib admissions (butlast/last/nth/\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.prompt.md:20:free-vars adaptation restored to upstream's (second def-env) shape, unfold-implicit try\ncollab/1793296786225-reviewer-hardening2.prompt.md:30:(.getMessage/ex-data paths); the meta-host-value mismatch disposition (upstream deviation\ncollab/1793294621496-compiler-engineer-hardening2.prompt.md:15:- test/yang/latte_oracle/ (manifest admission dispositions + fixture additions)\ncollab/1793294621496-compiler-engineer-hardening2.prompt.md:23:1. MANIFEST ADMISSION DISPOSITIONS: the manifest (test/yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn) records no admitted/excluded dispositions (the gate recorded :not-recorded-in-inherited-manifest). Extend the manifest schema and src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj so every binding carries :disposition :admitted | :excluded + :admission-reason, regenerate the table, and make the gate's coverage denominator read it. Admitted = reachable through the guest library + data module + admitted host seams (kind/*); excluded = genuinely nonportable (nano-time, pprint, host interop) with reasons. The gate-report format gains an honest admitted-vs-excluded denominator.\ncollab/1793294621496-compiler-engineer-hardening2.prompt.md:29:4. FREE-VARS CONTEXT ADAPTATION: the :free-vars-local-capture mismatch is an A/B adaptation bug — upstream free-vars reads local definitions via (second def-env), and the slice-8 context adaptation passes a context map in that position. Fix the adaptation so the verbatim upstream source sees the local-definitions shape it expects (a two-element structure matching upstream's global-defs/local-defs pair), not a redesign of upstream. Fixture: the gate's minimal repro must return #{x} on all lanes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"tail -14 docs/agents/known-gaps.md; sed -n '1540,1720p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; sed -n '1840,1940p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"  `bb test:routed src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc` run selected 61 JVM namespaces:\n  993 tests, 15,833 assertions, zero failures/errors; both runner scope records\n  reported exit 0 with `:gate-complete? false`. This is JVM feedback, not a\n  G2/G3 tri-host completion claim.\n- **TS-P3-03: closed.** `build-n-test.md` now names the Node REPL build\n  prerequisite (`build:yin-repl-node`) as the prerequisite that ensures\n  `bb deps:npm`.\n\nVerification: `bb -cp src/dev -m quick-sharded-test` passed 9 tests and 141\nassertions with zero failures/errors. Lint on the three changed Clojure files\nreported zero errors/warnings; `cljstyle check` passed. The requested\n`clj -M:kondo --lint src/dev` reported 31 errors and 27 warnings in unrelated\nfiles. Linting an archived `1fe3eb07` baseline produced identical findings;\nthose pre-existing Jolt/probe findings are outside this contract's file scope.\n\n\n(def ^:private kernel-sources\n  (into (into {} (map (juxt second identity)) kernel-declaration-refusals)\n        (map (fn [entry] [(kernel-guest-name (:symbol entry)) (kernel-source entry)])) kernel-entries))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-call\n  [form]\n  ;; Fixture code uses fully qualified names. Constructor adapters are the\n  ;; five existing context constructors, outside the 143-binding manifest.\n  (letfn [(rewrite\n            [x]\n            (cond\n              (and (seq? x) (= 'quote (first x))) x\n              (symbol? x) (if (and (namespace x) (str/starts-with? (namespace x) \"latte-kernel.\"))\n                            (if (str/starts-with? (name x) \"->\") (symbol (name x)) (kernel-guest-name x)) x)\n              (seq? x) (apply list (map rewrite x))\n              (vector? x) (mapv rewrite x)\n              (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(rewrite k) (rewrite v)])) x)\n              (set? x) (set (map rewrite x))\n              :else x))]\n    (rewrite form)))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-closure\n  [call]\n  (let [sources (merge (into {} (map (juxt second identity)) context-forms) kernel-sources)\n        mentions #(filter (set (keys sources)) (walk-symbols %))\n        needed (loop [todo (seq (mentions call)) seen #{}]\n                 (if-let [n (first todo)]\n                   (if (contains? seen n) (recur (next todo) seen)\n                       (recur (concat (next todo) (mentions (get sources n))) (conj seen n))) seen))\n        ordered (concat context-forms kernel-declaration-refusals (map #(get kernel-sources (kernel-guest-name (:symbol %))) kernel-entries))]\n    (filterv #(contains? needed (second %)) ordered)))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-fixture-call\n  [{:keys [call guest-call definitions project-proof?]} guest?]\n  (let [env (if guest? initial-context 'latte-kernel.defenv/empty-env)\n        register (if guest? 'register-definition 'latte-kernel.defenv/register-definition)\n        env (reduce (fn [env definition] (list register env (if guest? (kernel-call definition) definition))) env definitions)\n        call (if guest? (kernel-call (or guest-call call)) call)\n        call (if project-proof?\n               (list 'let ['r call] '(if (= :ok (first r)) [:ok (rest (second r))] r)) call)]\n    (list 'let ['env env] call)))\n\n\n(defn- evidence-data\n  \"EDN evidence retains all portable values and metadata. Nonportable host\n   payloads are explicit evidence, not accepted representation differences.\"\n  [x]\n  (cond\n    (fn? x) {:nonportable-host-value (str (class x))}\n    (record? x) (evidence-data (upstream-record-data x))\n    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(evidence-data k) (evidence-data v)])) x)\n    (vector? x) (mapv evidence-data x)\n    (set? x) (set (map evidence-data x))\n    (seq? x) (apply list (map evidence-data x))\n    :else x))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-attempt\n  [f]\n  (try (f)\n       (catch Exception e\n         {:status :blocked :message (ex-message e)\n          ;; Observer exceptions attach the entire host VM as :session. It is\n          ;; diagnostic machinery, not a portable domain payload; recursively\n          ;; expanding its closure environments duplicates the whole program.\n          :data (evidence-data (dissoc (ex-data e) :session))\n          :host-session-attached? (contains? (ex-data e) :session)\n          :causes (mapv (fn [cause] {:class (str (class cause)) :message (ex-message cause)})\n                        (take-while some? (iterate ex-cause e)))\n          :exception (str (class e))})))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-a\n  [fixture]\n  (kernel-attempt\n    #(let [value (cond\n                   (= :opacity-proof (:mode fixture))\n                   (let [outcome (a-opacity-proof (:script fixture))]\n                     (if (= :ok (first (:value outcome)))\n                       (update outcome :value (fn [v] [:ok (rest (second v))])) outcome))\n                   (= :unparser (:mode fixture))\n                   (with-redefs-fn {(upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/+unparser-registry+)\n                                    (atom {:fundamental [] :standard [] :user [] :unparsers {}})}\n                     (fn []\n                       ((upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/register-unparser!) :gate (eval (:extension fixture)))\n                       (a-leg (upstream-fn 'latte-kernel.unparser/unparse) [(:term fixture)])))\n                   :else (a-leg (eval (list 'fn [] (kernel-fixture-call fixture false))) []))]\n       {:status :completed :outcome (evidence-data value) :shape (result-shape (evidence-data value))})))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-c-program\n  [fixture]\n  (if (= :unparser (:mode fixture))\n    (list 'unparse (list 'register-unparser initial-context :gate (:extension fixture)) (list 'quote (:term fixture)))\n    (kernel-fixture-call fixture true)))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-b\n  [fixture]\n  (kernel-attempt\n    #(let [sandbox (create-ns (gensym \"kernel-gate-b-\"))\n           call (kernel-c-program fixture)\n           forms (kernel-closure call)\n           host-form (fn [form]\n                       ;; Preserve the actual one-argument gensym call. Only\n                       ;; the slice-8 explicit two-argument supply is adapted.\n                       (walk/postwalk\n                         (fn [x]\n                           (if (and (seq? x) (= 'gensym (first x)) (= 2 (count x)))\n                             (cons 'clojure.core/gensym (rest x)) x)) form))]\n       (try\n         (binding [*ns* sandbox]\n           (refer 'clojure.core)\n           (require '[clojure.set :refer [union difference]])\n           (eval (list* 'declare\n                        (concat (map second forms)\n                                (for [[ns-sym source] all-forms\n                                      form source :when (= 'declare (first form))\n                                      s (rest form)\n                                      :let [qualified (kernel-resolve ns-sym s)]\n                                      :when qualified]\n                                  (kernel-guest-name qualified)))))\n           (doseq [form forms] (eval (context-host-form (host-form form))))\n           (let [v (a-leg (eval (list 'fn [] (context-host-form (host-form call)))) [])]\n             {:status :completed :outcome (evidence-data v) :shape (result-shape (evidence-data v))}))\n         (finally (remove-ns (ns-name sandbox)))))))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-compile\n  [fixture]\n  (let [call (kernel-c-program fixture)\n        forms (kernel-closure call)\n        program (conj forms call)\n        program (into (yang/library-for program) program)\n        ast (yang/compile-program program true arg-vector-opts)\n        missing (unbound-ast-symbols ast program)]\n    (if (seq missing)\n      {:status :blocked :phase :admission :blocked-by (vec (sort missing))\n       :owners (into {} (for [s missing]\n                          [s (mapv second (filter #(some #{s} (tree-seq coll? seq %)) program))]))}\n      {:status :compiled :ast ast :forms forms})))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-c\n  [compiled lane]\n  (if (= :compiled (:status compiled))\n    (assoc (kernel-attempt\n             #(let [v (compiler-test/run-guest-ast (:ast compiled) (oracle-registry yang/kind-module) lane 1000000)]\n                {:status :completed :outcome (evidence-data v) :shape (result-shape (evidence-data v))}))\n           :lane lane)\n    (assoc compiled :lane lane)))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-row\n  [fixture]\n  (let [a (kernel-a fixture)\n        b (kernel-b fixture)\n        compiled (kernel-attempt #(kernel-compile fixture))\n        compiled (if (and (= :blocked (:status compiled)) (not (:blocked-by compiled)))\n                   (assoc compiled :phase :compile\n                          :blocked-by (if-let [n (get-in compiled [:data :name])] [n] [:compiler-exception])\n                          :minimal-source (get kernel-sources (get-in compiled [:data :name]))) compiled)\n        walker (kernel-c compiled :walker)\n        semantic (kernel-c compiled :semantic)\n        match? (and (= :completed (:status a) (:status b) (:status walker) (:status semantic))\n                    (= (:outcome a) (:outcome b))\n                    (agrees? (get a :outcome) (get walker :outcome))\n                    (= (:outcome walker) (:outcome semantic))\n                    (= (result-shape (:outcome a)) (result-shape (:outcome b)))\n                    (if (contains? (:outcome a) :value)\n                      (= (result-shape (:value (:outcome a)))\n                         (result-shape (second (:outcome walker))))\n                      (= (result-shape (get-in a [:outcome :thrown :data]))\n                         (result-shape (get-in walker [:outcome 1 :yin.k/data])))))\n        status (cond match? :pass\n                     (some #(= :blocked (:status %)) [a b walker semantic]) :blocked\n      (println \"KERNEL-BLOCKER\"\n               (pr-str {:id (:id row) :status (:status row)\n                        :blocked-by (get-in row [:c-walker :blocked-by])\n                        :a (get-in row [:a :status]) :b (get-in row [:b :status])\n                        :c-walker (get-in row [:c-walker :status])\n                        :c-semantic (get-in row [:c-semantic :status])})))\n    (is (= :pass (:gate-status evidence))\n        (str \"Kernel gate remains blocked: \" (:counts evidence)\n             \"; admitted/candidate but unexercised function/arities=\" (count (get-in evidence [:coverage :unexercised]))\n             \". See slice9_evidence.edn; blocked fixtures are not accepted negatives.\"))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
