lt-test {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]}\n           ;; DIAGNOSTIC only (-M:jolt:jolt-diag:jolt-test): a jolt stand-in\n           ;; for the corpus loader dao.jing.cbor-fixtures, whose root must\n           ;; precede test (src/dev/jolt_diag/dao/jing/cbor_fixtures.cljc);\n           ;; jolt puts :extra-paths roots first, in alias order (-Spath)\n           :jolt-diag {:extra-paths [\"src/dev/jolt_diag\"]}\n           :cljs-yin-repl\n           {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n                         reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n                         com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}\n            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.node-runner\"]}\n           :fmt {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                 :exec-fn tasks/fix-all}\n           ;; Build-time generation of the grammars-v4 Python3 parser.\n           ;; The tool version must equal the antlr4-runtime above.\n           :antlr-gen {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                       :extra-deps {org.antlr/antlr4 {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}}\n                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yang-antlr-gen\"]}\n           :kondo {:extra-deps {clj-kondo/clj-kondo {:mvn/version \"2026.01.19\"}}\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"clj-kondo.main\"]}\n           ;; Development/oracle only (datomic-q-v1 Client oracle runner,\n           ;; docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md); never a production\n           ;; dependency. Backend deps/config are pinned separately once selected.\n           :oracle {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\" \"test\"]\n                    :extra-deps {com.datomic/client-api {:mvn/version \"1.0.69\"}\n                                 ;; oracle backend: Datomic Local, in-process,\n                                 ;; run in docker/oracle (dev-scope only)\n                                 com.datomic/local {:mvn/version \"1.0.301\"}}}\n           :dbg {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                 :main-opts [\"-m\" \"debug-cljd\"]\n                 :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n           :cljd-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.runner\"]}\n           :cljd-yin-repl-build\n           {:main-opts  [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n            :cljd/opts  {:kind       :dart\n                         :main       yin.repl.main\n                         :output-dir \"build/yin-repl\"\n                         :output-to  \"build/yin-repl/yin_repl.dart\"}}\n           :dep-graph {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n                       :extra-deps {org.clojure/tools.namespace {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}}\n                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"dep-graph\"]}}}\n\n\n;; clj -X:fmt\n\n;; clj -M:nREPL\n\n;; clj -M:nREPL:server\n;; clj -M:test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-literal-test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-continuation-test\n;; clj -M:test -n yin.repl.python-antlr-test\n;; clj -X:test :nses '[yin.vm-literal-test yin.vm-test]'\n;; clj -M:test -v yin.vm-addition-test/test-lambda-with-multiple-operations\n\n;; clj -X:clean\n\n;; npx shadow-cljs compile test && node target/node-tests.js\n;; npx shadow-cljs release demo\n;; clj -M:dev -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile demo\n;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release demo\n\n\n;; mise exec -- clj -M:clojuredart:cljd watch \n;; mise exec -- flutter run \n\n;; To start the emulator:                                                                                              ;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34\n;; flutter emulators --launch Pixel_3_API_34\n;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34 -no-snapshot-load  \n;; emulator -list-avds\n\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph                    # full report + dep-graph.dot + dep-graph.svg\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph --filter \"yin.*\"   # only yin namespaces\n;;  clj -M:dep-graph --layout circo     # choose graphviz layout engine\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-29 18:23:08 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-30 01:23:08 +07\n\n# hardening2-review — commit 2292a068 (diff 7dc18478..2292a068)\n\n**Verdict: the round's claims are substantiated.** The 4→50 pass improvement on the unchanged 54-fixture baseline is produced by real guest machinery, not loosened fixtures; the admission inventory is sound and conservatively defaults new bindings to admitted; the 143 unexercised arities are honest accounting that independently keeps the gate open. Four P3 findings below; no P0–P2. The requested judgment on the kind/`var?` + `with-meta` departure: **justified, with two carried obligations**.\n\n## Findings\n\n**P3 | src/dev/latte_oracle_manifest.clj:50-57** | The stale manifest generator still rewrites `test/yang/latte_oracle/manifest.edn` in the old schema (no `:disposition`/`:admission-reason`), while `latte-oracle-tables/-main` (src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj:48-51) is now the writer of record. Running the old tool per its own docstring (`clj -M -m latte-oracle-manifest`) wipes the admission inventory from the working tree; the schema assertion in `test-oracle-classification` (test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:281-283) then fails loudly, but the checked-in inventory is lost and the old header comment is now false. | Fix: delete `latte-oracle-manifest` or reduce it to a delegation to `latte-oracle-tables`, and update its docstring.\n\n**P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:895-919** | The portable `try` lowerer's catch arm fires on *any* `[error-tag v]`: it binds `(data/nth outcome 1)` (line ~912) without discriminating the thrown value. A thrown non-ex-info value (e.g. `(throw \"boom\")` inside `(try … (catch Exception e …))`) is caught by the guest but propagates in Clojure (a thrown String is not an Exception). The catch-class guard (lines 903-905) constrains only the *syntax* of the clause, not the runtime class of the thrown value. Unexercised: all kernel sources throw ex-info only, and `test-portable-try-outcomes` (test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2024) tests ex-info throws exclusively. | Fix: either record the limitation in the library notes next to the other \"known compromises\" (clojure.cljc:1908-1916), or discriminate at runtime (catch only values carrying `:yin.k/message`, re-propagating others).\n\n**P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1163-1166** | Callable collections route through `invoke-value` only when the operator is a **local** or a **non-symbol** (`(or (contains? (locals env) operator) (not (symbol? operator)))`). A top-level defined collection — `(def v [1 2]) (v 0)` — compiles to a plain `:application` and errors at runtime instead of indexing, diverging from Clojure. Untested boundary of the \"callable collections\" admission (test/yang/clojure_test.clj:2049 uses only `let`-bound collections). | Fix: record as a known boundary in the library notes, or extend the route to operators in `::defined`.\n\n**P3 | src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1918-1926** | `kind-arities` publishes `'var? [1]` unconditionally (line 1926) while `kind-module` provides `var?` only under `#?(:clj … :default {})` (line 1920) — on a Node/Dart host the arity profile would admit a binding the module cannot supply. Relatedly, metadata attached via the new `kind/with-meta` seam has no stated serialization-survival guarantee: no fixture round-trips a meta'd value through the store/encoder, so `meta` after restoration is unspecified. | Fix: gate the published arity with the same reader conditional (or register the capability per-host at harness setup), and add a note/obligation that host metadata is not a serialized ABI field.\n\n## Requested judgment: the kind/seam departure\n\n`var?` (JVM predicate) and `with-meta` (host metadata write) as declared seams, instead of the requested guest-only implementation — **justified**:\n\n- `meta` (read) was **already** a `kind` seam at baseline (src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1883-1885 pre-diff); admitting the pure write on the same representation is coherent with the existing boundary. A second tagged representation would change symbol identity (`=`) and break every A-leg comparison involving symbols with metadata — including the `:minimal-with-meta` fixture, whose A leg runs host `with-meta`/`meta` via upstream Clojure.\n- `var?` is `:clj`-gated, carries no namespace lookup (`resolve` still refused at admission, tested at test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1312-1315), and the seam is exercised both guest-side (`:minimal-var`, both lanes) and host-side (`test-declared-var-seam`, line 1318).\n- Both are disclosed in three places: the gate md, the source comment (clojure.cljc:1878-1886), and evidence `:representation-seams`. The slice-8 admission test that previously rejected `var?` was changed *with* a replacement test — a declared policy change, not a silent loosening.\n\nConditions: findings 1's cross-host arity drift and the metadata-serialization obligation above should be tracked as explicit follow-ups before the owed Node/Dart lanes.\n\n## Adversarial priorities — what was checked and confirmed\n\n1. **Real agreement vs loosened fixtures.** The `match?` predicate (test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1709-1718) is byte-identical to baseline. The kernel_gate.edn diff deletes nothing and weakens no `:negative?`; it adds `:guest-call` to `:minimal-gensym-freshness`, and 3 new fixtures (57 total). The two adapted fixtures run a supply-threaded B/C program against the original A program — property-equivalent, recorded as `:adapted-call` in every evidence row and disclosed in the gate md. **First-hand rerun confirms:** 53 pass / 2 mismatch / 2 blocked / 57 attempted, 0 skipped.\n2. **Manifest admission soundness.** 155 bindings = 146 admitted + 9 excluded (verified by count in manifest.edn); all 9 exclusions are `defn`s with specific, true reasons (nano-time clock; pprint/stdout capture — verified against the pinned upstream sources). Excluded bindings compile to throwing `:nonportable-binding` stubs (latte_oracle_test.clj:1503-1507), so a fixture needing one blocks rather than silently passing. Nothing is excluded without reason (asserted at line 281-283). The declare-only `type-of-ascribe` is not in the manifest and is handled by a loud `:upstream-unbound` refusal; its row is honestly blocked on the A leg (JVM unbound-var throw, confirmed in the live rerun).\n3. **Gensym supply uniqueness.** Upstream's only live 1-arg `gensym` is `rebuild-type` (typing.cljc:474-477), faithfully adapted (`fresh-symbol` seeded from `:fresh`, result extended to `[result next-context]`); every upstream `let` whose init calls `rebuild-type` is automatically destructured to thread the next context (latte_oracle_test.clj:1437-1441); ambient prefix-only allocation is refused (clojure.cljc:2019-2023) and tested. Cross-context counter reuse remains possible only for a guest caller that drops the returned context — a documented convention, and no compiled upstream site does so.\n4. **free-vars restoration.** The upstream body is verbatim (its `(second def-env)` preserved; upstream syntax.cljc:204-228); the only addition is an argument-boundary `let` unwrapping a context map to its `:definitions` pair (latte_oracle_test.clj:1422-1429), accepting both shapes.\n5. **unfold-implicit coverage.** The actual upstream try/catch (typing.cljc:454-458) fits the lowered shape exactly (body + single `Exception`/`ExceptionInfo` catch, no finally). `.getMessage`/`ex-message`/`ex-data` are ported (clojure.cljc:682-686); every other dot-accessor is rejected at compile time (line 687-688), evidenced by the `.getStackTrace` refusal; nested try and operand-position throw are tested. The typed and throwing extension fixtures pass on all four legs.\n6. **Meta-host-value mismatches.** Recorded, not normalized: B's error data carries `{:nonportable-host-value \"class clojure.core$meta__5504\"}` while C carries `{:type :closure}`; agreement flags read `:a-b true, :a-c-walker false, :a-c-semantic false` — the deviation is left visible as a blocker.\n7. **143 unexercised arities.** Honest: `direct` counts only `:pass` rows' original calls (latte_oracle_test.clj:1746-1752); the denominator is the disposition inventory independent of fixture success; 165 − 22 = 143, each listed under `:coverage :unexercised`; the admitted+excluded partition of the 175 candidates is asserted (line 1831-1833). The only denominator shrinkage vs baseline is the 10 excluded arities — the disclosed admission change itself. The close-out test deliberately asserts `:pass` against a `:blocked` reality, keeping the suite red until the gate truly closes.\n\n## First-hand verification (this session, JVM)\n\n- `clj -M:test -n yang.clojure-test -n yin.vm.macro-test -n yang.clojure.stream-eval-test` → **119 tests, 1209 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**; plus `yin.vm.store-write-audit-test` → 3 tests / 129 assertions / 0 failures — combined **122 tests, 1,338 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors**, exactly the md's claim.\n- `clj -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test` → **23 tests, 997 assertions, 1 failure, 0 errors** — the single failure is the expected close-out gate; the live recount printed `{:pass 53, :blocked 2, :mismatch 2}, :fixture-count 57, :manifest-bindings 155, :function-arity-candidates 175` with 143 unexercised, matching slice9_evidence.edn and the md; the checked-in evidence was not rewritten by the run.\n\nNo file edits were made; this report is the sole deliverable.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
